// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/trinet/mint_authority.t27 -- who may mint TRI: the founder alone, with his own mint key, and only
; for admitted, verified work or a posted bounty, inside the emission schedule, on TON. Issue #8932
; (network MVP, see #8613; one minter, see #8618; identity, see #8869).
; --
; Owner decision, 2026-10-11 (Dmitrii Vasilev, GitHub gHashTag, account id 6774813), translated:
;   "Forbid anyone except me, gHashTag / Dmitrii Vasilev, to issue $TRI tokens. I am the solo
;   founder. Other developers earn $TRI through a win-win game I design."
; specs/trinet/tri-bridge.t27 already makes TON the chain of record and its minter the only one; it
; left open WHO may sign a mint (KEY_CUSTODY_AND_ATTESTOR_SET). This spec answers it for MINT, and
; tri-bridge.t27 v3 records the answer (MINT_KEY_HOLDER).
; --
; The rule (mint_check). A mint request is valid only if ALL of these hold, checked in this order; the
; first that fails is the reason code the minter refuses it with:
; 1. its minter is MINT_AUTHORITY_ACCOUNT, 6774813. Anyone else, the investor and every contributor
;    included, has no mint right (MR_NOT_AUTHORITY). Other developers earn TRI as the payees of mints,
;    never as minters.
; 2. its key is bound to that account as a fact of kind K_MINT_KEY, by specs/network/identity.t27's
;    binding rule (binding_valid, used as it is): a merged pull request that account authored, or a
;    signature by a signing key bound earlier to that account. A key bound to any other account is
;    refused even when that binding is valid, as a mint key or as a key registered for receipts or
;    commits (MR_KEY_NOT_AUTHORITY); the founder's own signing key is no mint key (MR_KEY_WRONG_KIND);
;    a founder mint key whose binding does not hold, e.g. one merged by someone else's pull request, is
;    refused (MR_KEY_BINDING_INVALID); a key no row binds, too (MR_KEY_UNBOUND).
; 3. its signature verifies under that key over mint_message (Ed25519, specs/tri/crypto/ed25519.t27
;    verify on the real bytes): the domain line MINT_HEAD, then minter, network, chain, nonce,
;    recipient, amount, kind and evidence, one line each (MR_BAD_SIGNATURE).
; 4. its chain is TON, the chain of record (tri-bridge.t27 mints_new_supply), and it names a TON network
;    (MR_NOT_TON); that network is this minter's own, so a testnet request never mints on mainnet
;    (MR_WRONG_MINTER).
; 5. its nonce is above every nonce this minter has accepted (MR_NONCE_REPLAYED), its amount is not 0
;    (MR_ZERO_AMOUNT), and the record of what it mints for has room (MR_LEDGER_FULL).
; 6. it names the evidence it rests on: the same payment kind, evidence id and payee (MR_EVIDENCE_MISMATCH),
;    and that (kind, evidence id) was never minted before (MR_EVIDENCE_SPENT).
; 7. the evidence is work: for a run fee (specs/verified/payout.t27 EXECUTOR_FEE, PROVIDER_FEE,
;    VERIFIER_FEE, AUTHOR_ROYALTY) an admitted run -- specs/network/quorum.t27 quorum_admits over the
;    trusted set, one vote per operator -- whose verdict is verified and referenced (payout() pays it
;    PAY_NORMAL), with an evidence id and the job's units in its billing nonce; for a BOUNTY, payout.t27
;    bounty_payable (the PR closes the task, is merged, its verdict verified) and an amount within the
;    posted one (MR_NO_WORK, MR_BOUNTY_OVER).
; 8. the amount fits the published emission schedule and the running total: specs/network/pool.t27's
;    emission_cap and halving. A run fee is at most its share (pool.t27's parts) of the grant the
;    schedule gives the job's units at the running total; a bounty at most what the cap leaves. A
;    schedule whose cap passes tri-bridge.t27 CAP_MTRI is no schedule (MR_NO_SCHEDULE, MR_OVER_SCHEDULE).
; mint_apply records an accepted mint: the running total, the nonce, the spent (kind, evidence id).
; --
; The key custody answer (tri-bridge.t27 KEY_CUSTODY_AND_ATTESTOR_SET, for MINT): the founder holds the
; mint key. The attestors and validators are not appointed by it: they stay a protocol k-of-n
; (quorum.t27), one vote per operator, and admit the work a mint rests on. Holding the mint key gives no
; vote, and votes give no mint: a mint needs both the founder's signature and the quorum's admission.
; --
; Today: the network's table (identity.t27 identity_table) binds no mint key, and no emission schedule
; is published (SCHEDULE_BASE_RATE and SCHEDULE_HALVING_EVERY are 0), so every mint is refused. The
; founder publishes both by pull requests he authors; this file chooses no rate.
; Hosts (to come, each checked against this spec's vectors): the TON minter contract (FunC) and
; src/trinet/mint_authority.zig in gHashTag/trinity-fpga.
; Claim status: DESIGN. The honest limits: the evidence (votes, verified, referenced, posted) is what
; the quorum and the ledger attest, given to the minter, not recomputed here; a pull request's author is
; GitHub's fact (identity.t27). Ed25519 here makes no constant-time claim (ed25519.t27); it signs only
; the fixture seeds in tests, whose seeds are public, so those keys prove nothing outside the tests.
; ASCII only (L3).
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module TrinetMintAuthority;

use tri::crypto::ed25519;
use network::identity;
use network::quorum;
use network::pool;
use verified::payout;
use trinet::tri-bridge;

/// The one account that may mint: gHashTag, Dmitrii Vasilev, the founder.
pub const MINT_AUTHORITY_ACCOUNT : u64 = 6774813;

/// The identity fact kind of a mint key: an Ed25519 public key, SIGNING_KEY_HEX hex digits, next after
/// identity.t27's K_EMAIL, K_RECEIPT_KEY, K_SIGNING_KEY and K_FUSE_DNA. Its rows are IdentityTable rows
/// and bind by binding_valid, like every other fact.
pub const K_MINT_KEY : u8 = 5;

/// The domain line of a mint request's signed message.
pub const MINT_HEAD : str = "t27-tri-mint-v1";

/// The published emission schedule: none yet. The founder publishes it by a pull request he authors.
pub const SCHEDULE_BASE_RATE : u64 = 0;
pub const SCHEDULE_HALVING_EVERY : u64 = 0;

/// The fixed size of a minter's record of spent evidence.
pub const SPENT_ROWS : u32 = 16;

/// mint_check() answers. MR_OK mints; every other code refuses.
pub const MR_OK : u8 = 0;
pub const MR_NOT_AUTHORITY : u8 = 1;
pub const MR_KEY_UNBOUND : u8 = 2;
pub const MR_KEY_NOT_AUTHORITY : u8 = 3;
pub const MR_KEY_WRONG_KIND : u8 = 4;
pub const MR_KEY_BINDING_INVALID : u8 = 5;
pub const MR_BAD_SIGNATURE : u8 = 6;
pub const MR_NOT_TON : u8 = 7;
pub const MR_WRONG_MINTER : u8 = 8;
pub const MR_NONCE_REPLAYED : u8 = 9;
pub const MR_ZERO_AMOUNT : u8 = 10;
pub const MR_LEDGER_FULL : u8 = 11;
pub const MR_EVIDENCE_MISMATCH : u8 = 12;
pub const MR_EVIDENCE_SPENT : u8 = 13;
pub const MR_NO_WORK : u8 = 14;
pub const MR_BOUNTY_OVER : u8 = 15;
pub const MR_NO_SCHEDULE : u8 = 16;
pub const MR_OVER_SCHEDULE : u8 = 17;
pub const MR_CODES : u8 = 17;

invariant mint_authority_is_the_founder_and_its_codes_are_distinct {
    assert MINT_AUTHORITY_ACCOUNT == MINT_KEY_HOLDER;
    assert K_MINT_KEY != K_EMAIL and K_MINT_KEY != K_RECEIPT_KEY and K_MINT_KEY != K_SIGNING_KEY and K_MINT_KEY != K_FUSE_DNA;
    assert MR_OK == 0 and MR_NOT_AUTHORITY == 1 and MR_OVER_SCHEDULE == MR_CODES;
    assert CHAIN_OF_RECORD == CHAIN_TON;
}

// --- The request, the evidence, the schedule, the minter's record ---------------------------------

/// A mint request: who signs it, with which key, for which network and chain, under which nonce, to
/// whom, how much (mTRI), and the payment kind and evidence id it rests on. sig is over mint_message.
pub struct MintRequest {
    minter: u64,
    key: [32]u8,
    network: str,
    chain: u8,
    nonce: u64,
    recipient: u64,
    amount: u64,
    kind: u8,
    evidence: u64,
    sig: [64]u8,
}

/// What the quorum and the ledger attest about the work: the payment kind, its evidence id (the
/// admitted run for a run fee, the agreeing receipt for a verifier fee, the task for a bounty), the
/// payee, the job's billing nonce (payout.t27: its units in the low bits), the key ids of the receipts
/// that agree on the run, the agreeing verifier operators other than the executor's own (pool.t27
/// job_split), the verdict's state, and a bounty's posted amount and task state.
pub struct WorkEvidence {
    kind: u8,
    id: u64,
    payee: u64,
    job_nonce: u64,
    voters: [8]u64,
    votes: u32,
    verifiers: u64,
    verified: bool,
    referenced: bool,
    posted: u64,
    closes_task: bool,
    merged: bool,
}

/// An emission schedule: pool.t27's base rate and halving step.
pub struct MintSchedule {
    base_rate: u64,
    halving_every: u64,
}

/// What a minter keeps: its own network, the running total minted, the highest nonce it accepted and
/// the (kind, evidence id) pairs it minted for.
pub struct MintState {
    network: str,
    minted: u64,
    last_nonce: u64,
    spent: u32,
    spent_kind: [16]u8,
    spent_id: [16]u64,
}

pub fn published_schedule() -> MintSchedule {
    return MintSchedule { base_rate: SCHEDULE_BASE_RATE, halving_every: SCHEDULE_HALVING_EVERY };
}

/// A minter that has minted nothing, on network `net`.
pub fn mint_state_new(net: string) -> MintState {
    return MintState { network: net, minted: 0, last_nonce: 0, spent: 0, spent_kind: [0; 16], spent_id: [0; 16] };
}

/// Is `net` a TON network (CAIP-2), mainnet or testnet?
pub fn is_ton_network(net: string) -> bool {
    return id_span_eq(net, 0, net.len, NET_TON_MAINNET) or id_span_eq(net, 0, net.len, NET_TON_TESTNET);
}

/// The bytes a mint request signs: MINT_HEAD, then `minter`, `network`, `chain`, `nonce`, `recipient`,
/// `amount`, `kind` and `evidence`, each a line.
pub fn mint_message(req: MintRequest) -> IdMessage {
    var m : IdMessage = IdMessage { bytes: [0; 512], used: 0 };
    m = idm_text(m, MINT_HEAD, true);
    m = idm_text(m, "minter ", false);
    m = idm_dec(m, req.minter);
    m = idm_text(m, "network ", false);
    m = idm_text(m, req.network, true);
    m = idm_text(m, "chain ", false);
    m = idm_dec(m, req.chain as u64);
    m = idm_text(m, "nonce ", false);
    m = idm_dec(m, req.nonce);
    m = idm_text(m, "recipient ", false);
    m = idm_dec(m, req.recipient);
    m = idm_text(m, "amount ", false);
    m = idm_dec(m, req.amount);
    m = idm_text(m, "kind ", false);
    m = idm_dec(m, req.kind as u64);
    m = idm_text(m, "evidence ", false);
    m = idm_dec(m, req.evidence);
    return m;
}

/// Is `key` a mint key of the founder, validly bound? MR_OK when some row binds it so; otherwise why
/// not. Only rows whose value is a well-formed key are compared, so no email or id matches a key.
pub fn mint_key_status(tab: IdentityTable, key: [32]u8) -> u8 {
    var founder_bad : bool = false;
    var other : bool = false;
    var wrong_kind : bool = false;
    var i : u32 = 0;
    while (i < tab.bindings and i < ID_ROWS) {
        const v : string = tab.b_value[i];
        if (signing_key_ok(v) and bytes32_eq(id_hex32(v, 0), key)) {
            const a : u64 = binding_account(tab, i);
            if (a != MINT_AUTHORITY_ACCOUNT) { other = true; }
            if (a == MINT_AUTHORITY_ACCOUNT and tab.b_kind[i] != K_MINT_KEY) { wrong_kind = true; }
            if (a == MINT_AUTHORITY_ACCOUNT and tab.b_kind[i] == K_MINT_KEY) {
                if (binding_valid(tab, i)) { return MR_OK; }
                founder_bad = true;
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (founder_bad) { return MR_KEY_BINDING_INVALID; }
    if (other) { return MR_KEY_NOT_AUTHORITY; }
    if (wrong_kind) { return MR_KEY_WRONG_KIND; }
    return MR_KEY_UNBOUND;
}

/// Has this minter minted for (kind, id) before?
pub fn evidence_spent(st: MintState, kind: u8, id: u64) -> bool {
    var k : u32 = 0;
    while (k < st.spent and k < SPENT_ROWS) {
        if (st.spent_kind[k] == kind and st.spent_id[k] == id) { return true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    return false;
}

/// Is the evidence admitted, verified work for a run fee: a known run-fee kind, an evidence id, the
/// job's units, the trusted quorum's admission by operator votes, and a verified, referenced verdict?
pub fn work_admitted(ev: WorkEvidence) -> bool {
    if (payment_kind_known(ev.kind) == false or ev.kind == BOUNTY) { return false; }
    if (ev.id == 0 or nonce_units(ev.job_nonce) == 0) { return false; }
    if (ev.kind == VERIFIER_FEE and ev.verifiers == 0) { return false; }
    const c : QuorumConfig = trusted_config();
    if (quorum_admits(c, operator_votes(c, ev.voters, ev.votes)) == false) { return false; }
    return payout(OUT_CREDITED, ev.verified, ev.referenced) == PAY_NORMAL;
}

/// A run fee's parts of POOL_PARTS (pool.t27); 0 for any other kind.
pub fn kind_parts(kind: u8) -> u64 {
    if (kind == EXECUTOR_FEE) { return EXECUTOR_PARTS; }
    if (kind == PROVIDER_FEE) { return PROVIDER_PARTS; }
    if (kind == AUTHOR_ROYALTY) { return AUTHOR_PARTS; }
    if (kind == VERIFIER_FEE) { return VERIFIER_BASE_PARTS; }
    return 0;
}

/// A schedule a mint can be judged by: a rate, a halving step, and a cap within tri-bridge.t27's.
pub fn schedule_published(s: MintSchedule) -> bool {
    if (s.base_rate == 0 or s.halving_every == 0) { return false; }
    return emission_cap(s.base_rate, s.halving_every) <= CAP_MTRI;
}

/// The most this evidence may mint at the running total `minted`: a run fee's share of the grant the
/// schedule gives the job's units there; a bounty's posted amount, cut at what the cap leaves.
pub fn mint_room(ev: WorkEvidence, s: MintSchedule, minted: u64) -> u64 {
    const cap : u64 = emission_cap(s.base_rate, s.halving_every);
    if (ev.kind == BOUNTY) { return emission_grant(ev.posted, minted, cap); }
    const grant : u64 = emission_grant(emission_want(nonce_units(ev.job_nonce), s.base_rate, minted, s.halving_every), minted, cap);
    if (ev.kind == VERIFIER_FEE) {
        if (ev.verifiers == 0) { return 0; }
        return part_of(grant, VERIFIER_BASE_PARTS) / ev.verifiers;
    }
    return part_of(grant, kind_parts(ev.kind));
}

/// The rule: MR_OK when the request may mint, else the first reason it may not.
pub fn mint_check(tab: IdentityTable, req: MintRequest, ev: WorkEvidence, s: MintSchedule, st: MintState) -> u8 {
    if (req.minter != MINT_AUTHORITY_ACCOUNT) { return MR_NOT_AUTHORITY; }
    const ks : u8 = mint_key_status(tab, req.key);
    if (ks != MR_OK) { return ks; }
    const m : IdMessage = mint_message(req);
    if (verify(req.key, m.bytes[0..m.used], req.sig) == false) { return MR_BAD_SIGNATURE; }
    if (mints_new_supply(req.chain) == false or is_ton_network(req.network) == false) { return MR_NOT_TON; }
    if (id_span_eq(req.network, 0, req.network.len, st.network) == false) { return MR_WRONG_MINTER; }
    if (req.nonce <= st.last_nonce) { return MR_NONCE_REPLAYED; }
    if (req.amount == 0) { return MR_ZERO_AMOUNT; }
    if (st.spent >= SPENT_ROWS) { return MR_LEDGER_FULL; }
    if (req.kind != ev.kind or req.evidence != ev.id or req.recipient != ev.payee) { return MR_EVIDENCE_MISMATCH; }
    if (evidence_spent(st, req.kind, req.evidence)) { return MR_EVIDENCE_SPENT; }
    if (ev.kind == BOUNTY) {
        if (ev.id == 0 or bounty_payable(ev.closes_task, ev.merged, ev.verified, false) == false) { return MR_NO_WORK; }
        if (req.amount > ev.posted) { return MR_BOUNTY_OVER; }
    }
    if (ev.kind != BOUNTY and work_admitted(ev) == false) { return MR_NO_WORK; }
    if (schedule_published(s) == false) { return MR_NO_SCHEDULE; }
    if (req.amount > mint_room(ev, s, st.minted)) { return MR_OVER_SCHEDULE; }
    return MR_OK;
}

/// The minter's record after it mints `req`: the running total, the nonce, the spent evidence.
pub fn mint_apply(st: MintState, req: MintRequest) -> MintState {
    var o : MintState = st;
    if (o.spent >= SPENT_ROWS) { return o; }
    o.minted = o.minted + req.amount;
    o.last_nonce = req.nonce;
    o.spent_kind[o.spent] = req.kind;
    o.spent_id[o.spent] = req.evidence;
    o.spent = o.spent + 1;
    return o;
}

; --- Fixtures ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Three accounts: the founder 6774813 (fixture keys, NOT his real keys), bob 202 (a contributor) and
; investor 404. Seeds are identity.t27's fixture_seed(k), public; the public keys and signatures were
; computed with PyNaCl 1.5 when the tests were written, and the tests derive and sign them again with
; ed25519.t27 and must get the same bytes.
;   row 0 founder  mint key    MK1 seed 21  EV_PR #9101 by the founder        valid
;   row 1 founder  signing key SK  seed 22  EV_PR #9101 by the founder        valid (no mint key)
;   row 2 founder  mint key    MK2 seed 23  EV_SIGNED by row 1 (SK)           valid, a chain of two
;   row 3 bob      mint key    BK  seed 24  EV_PR #9102 by bob                valid, but bob's
;   row 4 bob      signing key BS  seed 25  EV_PR #9102 by bob                valid, registered for receipts
;   row 5 founder  mint key    MK3 seed 26  EV_PR #9102: bob's pull request   refused
;   row 6 investor mint key    IK  seed 27  EV_PR #9103 by the investor       valid, but the investor's
;   row 7 founder  mint key    MK4 seed 28  EV_SIGNED by row 4: bob's key     refused
; Seed 29's key is bound by no row.

pub const MX_MK1 : str = "6ac1724d65f92b613b79bcc1c5d53c8c50f2f3fb273a605698f9db1d2e10dc4d";
pub const MX_SK : str = "08cb3945b683392aecfd0e499f231cf223043c3de14b991521711dfeb08ed459";
pub const MX_MK2 : str = "56963f686af80f48a3f4660be60832ba87fdca14302bd414f4d0f5a8ce115edb";
pub const MX_BK : str = "602228bf62734af426d114b53b9e8624ae3bb31ef7718debd91fea62952668d0";
pub const MX_BS : str = "c85e0390c4299e443356af522e4d82cebf611fe5a0892ae349f1d684b11cbde4";
pub const MX_MK3 : str = "04056d28f81d62d6cb9e2c15d8eb2532003b42a6e93ea26f572af4bafc0f2db0";
pub const MX_IK : str = "1c94b449089cefde4301fa33cf2cc94a62c4ab3b7b4892f9da979e2df5ea4c13";
